@DBKent 🤔. Would you mind joining our TiDB Community Slack chatroom (https://pingcap.com/tidbslack) for real-time investigation? You could DM me (`@kennytm`) there. (We could also use WeChat if you like)

If you prefer to continue here, could you check 

1. Whether all of the following return the same values? (this checks if it is caused by case-sensitivity)

    ```sql
    ADMIN CHECKSUM TABLE FastREportDB5;
    --                        ^ note the capital E
    ADMIN CHECKSUM TABLE `ReportDB`.`FastREportDB5`;
    ```

2. Insert a single row into the table. Is the CHECKSUM changed? (this checks if the table range is lost)

    ```sql
    INSERT INTO FastREportDB5 VALUES ( ... );
    SELECT count(1) FROM FastREportDB5;
    -- should become 40226103

    ADMIN CHECKSUM TABLE FastREportDB5;
    -- the normal case should return `Total_kvs = 241356618`
    -- the abnormal case could return `Total_kvs = 0` or `Total_kvs = 6`.
    ```

3. Is the checksum mismatch still reproducible if we drop the table `FastREportDB5`, and only import 10 rows through Lightning? (this checks if the error is caused by data or schema)

Thanks!

After a discussion on Slack, we have determined the real cause of this issue is that **ADMIN CHECKSUM does not support partitioned tables**.

```sql
create table a(a int) partition by hash(a) partitions 5;
insert into a values (1), (2), (3);
admin checksum table a;
-- returns 0 checksum
```
